    a: "Eric Bristow won the most BDO World Professional Darts Championships, capturing five titles in 1980, 1981, 1984, 1985, and 1986."
  },
  {
    q: "Who was the last BDO world champion?",
    a: "Wayne Warren of Wales was the final BDO world champion, winning the 2020 championship at Indigo at The O2 by defeating Jim Williams 7–4 on 12 January 2020."
  },
  {
    q: "What happened to the BDO?",
    a: "The British Darts Organisation collapsed in 2020 following decades of commercial decline, falling TV revenues, and severe financial insolvency. After drastically cutting player prize money at the 2020 World Championship, the company went into formal liquidation in September 2020."
  },
  {
    q: "Did Phil Taylor play in the BDO?",
    a: "Yes. Phil Taylor began his professional career in the BDO under the mentorship of Eric Bristow, winning two BDO World Championships in 1990 and 1992 before leading the breakaway to form the PDC in 1993."
  },
  {
    q: "Where was the BDO World Championship held?",
    a: "The tournament was held at the Heart of the Midlands Club in Nottingham (1978), the Jollees Club in Stoke-on-Trent (1979–1985), the Lakeside Country Club in Frimley Green (1986–2019), and Indigo at The O2 in London for its final 2020 edition."
